title: Presence and absence
tags: Query
kind: reference
aliases: present absent unknown
summary: IS PRESENT, IS ABSENT and IS UNKNOWN tell a value, an explicit nothing and a missing field apart.

|!Predicate |!Matches |
|`field IS PRESENT` |the field has a value that is not `nothing` |
|`field IS ABSENT` |the field is set to `nothing` — an explicit "does not apply" |
|`field IS UNKNOWN` |the field was never set on this metarecord |

A deleted file's metarecord has `mfr_path IS ABSENT` (the path was set to `nothing`),
not `UNKNOWN`. Why the two absences are kept apart: [[Nothing versus unknown]].

A `nothing` row never matches a value comparison: `rating != 3` does not match a
metarecord whose `rating` is `nothing` or unknown — `!=` is not the complement of
`=`. "Not 3, or no rating" is `NOT rating = 3`. A comparison ''with'' `nothing` is
refused ([[Comparisons]]): absence is asked with these three.

Under an aspect the same words read one level down: `path:parent IS ABSENT` matches
the nodes whose parent is absent — the roots of a forest ([[Field aspects]]). An aspect
on `IS UNKNOWN` is refused: there is no row, so no component to read.
